  "title": "Tuna stuffed tomatoes",
  "description": "Choose small-sized tomatoes if you want to make a starter out of this recipe, or cherry tomatoes to serve as an appetizer.",
  "editorial": {
    "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Here is my recipe for tuna-stuffed tomatoes with mayonnaise. Choose small-sized tomatoes if you want to make an appetizer out of this recipe, and cherry tomatoes to serve as an appetizer.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe {\"id\":28330,\"template\":\"chic-template-english\",\"updated\":1714865703374} -->\n<!--WPRM Recipe 28330-->\n<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe\">\n\t<h2 class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-name\">Tuna stuffed tomatoes</h2>\n\t<img class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-image\" src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/IMG_5293.Blog_-150x150.png\"/>\t<p class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-summary\">\n\t\t<p>Choose small-sized tomatoes if you want to make a starter out of this recipe, or cherry tomatoes to serve as an appetizer.</p>\t</p>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-equipment\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-ingredients\">\n\t\t<ul><li>180  g canned tuna (drained)</li><li>1 hard-boiled egg (peeled)</li><li>2 tablespoons mayonnaise</li><li>2-3 tablespoons lemon juice</li><li>Salt and pepper</li><li>4 small-sized tomatoes or 24 cherry tomatoes</li></ul>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-instructions\">\n\t\t<ol><li><p>Mash the tuna using a fork.</p><br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/IMG_5239.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li><p>Grate the egg (or crush it with a fork).</p><br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/IMG_5242.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li><p>Mix the tuna with the egg and mayonnaise.</p><br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/IMG_5243.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li><p>Drizzle with lemon juice.</p><br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/IMG_5248.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li><p>Season with salt and pepper.</p><br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/IMG_5264.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li><p>Cut the tops off the tomatoes to form a lid. Hollow them out without damaging the skin.</p><br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/IMG_3607.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li><p>Stuff the tomatoes (with the tuna mixture) and close the lids.</p><br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/IMG_5269.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li><p>Cherry tomatoes take longer to stuff, but they will make an impression at a party. ;)</p><br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/IMG_5695.Blog_-1-150x150.png\"/><br /></li></ol>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-notes\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta\">\n\t\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta-course\">Appetizer</div><div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta-cuisine\">Français, French, Italian, Italien</div><div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta-keyword\">tomates farcies, tomates farcies au fromage, tomato, tomatoes stuffed, tomatoes stuffed with tuna</div>\t</div>\n</div>\n<!--End WPRM Recipe-->\n<!-- /wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe -->",
    "excerpt": "Tomatoes stuffed with tuna"
  },
